<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:55Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Mark Carney's EU speech highlights Canada's shifting alliances</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:028fecc8b5ef36bf3ef541c2f06ec22537cf7a38583a8bcb3f03b2a594b9433a</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:37:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mark-carney-s-eu-speech-highlights-canada-s-shifting-alliances-1--377245a8049c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mark-carney-s-eu-speech-highlights-canada-s-shifting-alliances-1" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney addressed the European Parliament as Ottawa and Brussels deepen ties against a backdrop of strained relations with the United States. FRANCE 24's Doug Herbert explains how the speech illustrates a broader shift in alliances, with a message that, until recently, would more likely have been delivered in Washington than Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Congress passes Russia sanctions bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f3beaab9b2c22d240122b7335f4c8916c1942b020ba29b4df18c41afb2dce52</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T10:26:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-congress-passes-russia-sanctions-bill--56b085a39b53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/us-congress-passes-russia-sanctions-bill" /><summary type="html">The US Congress has approved a sweeping Russia sanctions bill, sending it to President Donald Trump for final approval as Washington seeks to increase pressure on Moscow over the war in Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>US again denies Palestinian leader visa for UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16e0bebfcc1b6a35d4d893d579355486c8c497db412ee225dbcac28e19a09137</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T03:03:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260917-us-palestinian-leader-visa-un-general-assembly-new-york--07c18cfc3fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260917-us-palestinian-leader-visa-un-general-assembly-new-york" /><summary type="html">The United States has denied Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas a visa to attend next week's UN General Assembly in New York, a source familiar with the matter said on Wednesday. The State Department separately said it would deny visas to Palestinian officials, citing failures to reform and actions it said undermined peace prospects.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US House holds billionaire Epstein associate Leon Black in contempt of Congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81a924c9607c39deb0058bd0b02c76044cb512fcb7b565ce55061bee3fc6da6d</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T22:37:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-leon-black-epstein-contempt-congress--b3c6fcbe094a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-leon-black-epstein-contempt-congress" /><summary type="html">The US House of Representatives on Wednesday held billionaire investor Leon Black in contempt of Congress for defying two subpoenas in its investigation into sex offender Jeffrey Epstein. The measure passed by unanimous consent and will be referred to the Justice Department, which will decide whether to pursue criminal charges.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US announces charges against five alleged agents for Russia over assassination plots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad85815b628bf525ef6ee7afb7d9532f0cddf592f6ef6d2c428b14a9496a9a91</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:13:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-us-announces-charges-against-five-alleged-agents-for-russia-over-assassination-plots--d063e095b8a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-us-announces-charges-against-five-alleged-agents-for-russia-over-assassination-plots" /><summary type="html">The US Department of Justice announced on Tuesday charges against five alleged Russian intelligence agents accused of recruiting a global network to conspire attacks and carry out assassinations by order of the Kremlin. The suspects remain at large.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran's tour in trouble after Pro-Palestine acts drop out</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6148e6bd0a75fb1c03dafce77eaa4898b584ae34dec9fa059731e12235926245</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T06:54:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-ed-sheeran-s-tour-in-trouble-after-pro-palestine-acts-drop-out--fa91bae8f5f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-ed-sheeran-s-tour-in-trouble-after-pro-palestine-acts-drop-out" /><summary type="html">More artists scheduled to participate in Ed Sheeran’s tour of North and South America have quit in solidarity with the rapper Macklemore, who was dropped for making pro-Palestinian comments onstage. Among them are Irish acts Rowe and Lukas Graham, as well as Billie Eilish’s brother, Finneas.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>NBC news helicopter crashes in LA while covering bus collision, killing three</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d7d8e23fc3393e45289ed2ebf4fd006fca2577e932779ec40aaf7a4f4a10ff6</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T04:47:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-media-helicopter-crashes-in-la-while-covering-bus-collision-killing-three--9853922e6c26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-media-helicopter-crashes-in-la-while-covering-bus-collision-killing-three" /><summary type="html">A news helicopter covering a deadly bus crash in the Los Angeles neighbourhood of Chatsworth came down on Tuesday, killing three people, including a pedestrian.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>New French ambassador to US cleared to take up post after diplomatic spat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcbd2cdf8e9738d6f6479be640d5145c576db3ed4a48cee2b694bf2817b13d99</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T03:10:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-new-french-ambassador-to-us-cleared-to-take-up-post-after-diplomatic-spat--e89865bec267.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-new-french-ambassador-to-us-cleared-to-take-up-post-after-diplomatic-spat" /><summary type="html">France's incoming ambassador to the US has been cleared to take up his post after Paris apologised for criticism of Washington over a UN vote. Aurélien Lechevallier, chosen by President Emmanuel Macron to replace Laurent Bili, is expected to arrive in Washington in the coming weeks following the diplomatic dispute.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says renovation of Kennedy Center depends on whether his name is on it</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d80a46142f55169e607b4c9903bbf7183cd7066bcb329142e587bca74eacbdf</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T22:19:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-trump-threatens-to-not-reopen-kennedy-center-after-board-blocks-renaming--2d9a7916d6f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-trump-threatens-to-not-reopen-kennedy-center-after-board-blocks-renaming" /><summary type="html">The Kennedy Center board voted Tuesday to close most of the Washington performing arts complex for safety repairs, hours after a judge again blocked efforts to add President Donald Trump’s name to the building. Trump said the $257 million renovation plan depended on recognising his role in the project.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Canada can offer a more reliable route for energy exports to the EU', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e38829b200ef8bee375a1bf418b196ce536de0a74b29030592c27512de349f2e</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:42:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canada-can-offer-a-more-reliable-route-for-energy-exports-to-the-eu-expert-says--5f8600ea249f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/canada-can-offer-a-more-reliable-route-for-energy-exports-to-the-eu-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Dr. Walaa-Eldeen Bakry, Principal Lecturer in Project Management and Finance and Director of Executive Education at Westminster Business School, says that "Carney is deliberately aiming to diversify the Canadian trade policy", explaining that it "can actually offer a more reliable route in terms of energy exports from Canada into the EU and we have seen last year a significant increase in oil exports to some European countries".</summary></entry><entry><title>'Revolutionary change in US foreign policy: MAGA does not see itself as leader of democratic world'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ada526e1442123693761c82dc44e7fbc05eadfb3c552ee3f5f8d2487a874bb41</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:18:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-revolutionary-change-in-american-foreign-policy-canada-pivoting-towards-eu-india-and-china--5811b0689e1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-revolutionary-change-in-american-foreign-policy-canada-pivoting-towards-eu-india-and-china" /><summary type="html">For Spotlight, FRANCE 24 François Picard is pleased to welcome Anne Applebaum, staff writer at The Atlantic and author of Autocracy, Inc. According to Applebaum, the upheaval in American diplomacy and foreign policy transcends any one administration. She describes a full-fledged transformation in the way the United States exerts power, pivoting away from leadership of a democratic alliance and toward a transactional, mafia-style politics that fuses ideology, private economic interests, personal relationships and geopolitical leverage.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's Carney seeks closer Europe ties to counter hostile US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cf5b2b32d0c2723bcb4bfd955e88fe35ca42cff44e5b06b37fd43cde2f9aeee</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T18:57:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canada-s-carney-seeks-closer-europe-ties-to-counter-hostile-us--1cc68ad20b35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/canada-s-carney-seeks-closer-europe-ties-to-counter-hostile-us" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney is heading to Europe in the middle of a trade war with U.S. President Donald Trump, seeking a deeper relationship with the European Union that could give Canadians greater freedom to work and study there. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.</summary></entry><entry><title>US acknowledges for the first time that it has deployed weapons in space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1e0c9f0105c66919ecddc99dfa8289154ac35ea796de1c156161df1e58cab67</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T18:34:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-acknowledges-for-the-first-time-that-it-has-deployed-weapons-in-space--0f22fd99aebc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/us-acknowledges-for-the-first-time-that-it-has-deployed-weapons-in-space" /><summary type="html">The United States has confirmed for the first time that it has deployed weapons in space, a remarkable revelation after previous warnings about countries such as Russia possibly weaponizing a global frontier long agreed in treaties to be used for only peaceful purposes. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rapid data center expansion incites backlash in Republican stronghold</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10ce03b75f3f00ca84c013411a1b7784a0d6ff95aa90605591bea32b6f4a8dac</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T15:05:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260915-rapid-data-center-expansion-incites-backlash-in-republican-stronghold--12576b212a35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260915-rapid-data-center-expansion-incites-backlash-in-republican-stronghold" /><summary type="html">With just a couple months to go until the US midterm election, a new political fault line is emerging in Republican strongholds across Texas driven by the rapid expansion of artificial intelligence. According to an analysis by the Texas Tribune, nearly 60 percent of planned new data centers are set to be built in congressional districts that voted for Donald Trump in 2024. But the AI boom is now sparking a backlash from some of the voters who helped put him back in office. Pierrick Leurent and Valérie Defert have this report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Corruption ‘endemic’ in Trump administration: 'Checks and balances only in effect at lower courts'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4abf9f7600354a59fb23ccea7fcc3a0f25eba0a5c94c8c6337129a1ee6d70e41</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:52:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-corruption-endemic-in-trump-administration-checks-and-balances-only-in-effect-at-lower-cour--944e7a2db01b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-corruption-endemic-in-trump-administration-checks-and-balances-only-in-effect-at-lower-courts" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Andrew Weissmann, Author, Professor at NYU School of Law, and former General Counsel of the FBI. He argues that as political deception and deliberate falsehoods become normalized, and politically useful, it erodes any trust we have in our government and our institutions. Drawing on his book, "Liar’s Kingdom", Weissmann questions why political leaders are above the law in the United States, while ordinary citizens risk serious legal consequences for making intentionally false statements.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war exposes US munitions shortfall, industrial bottlenecks, Pentagon report says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:787bad371003daa32bc2f59fd4933ca9ec9612b6d128d008e0d4b4052d329f2c</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T06:07:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-iran-war-exposes-us-munitions-shortfall-industrial-bottlenecks-pentagon-report-says--8ac2e20850a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-iran-war-exposes-us-munitions-shortfall-industrial-bottlenecks-pentagon-report-says" /><summary type="html">The US military faces shortages of key munitions due to the Iran war and industrial "bottlenecks" to rebuild stockpiles, a Pentagon watchdog warned in a report published on Monday, contradicting US President Donald Trump's assurances that ammunition supplies are "virtually unlimited".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela to join G20 energy talks in Texas at US invitation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a92cdaf7dd935eea7549cdd930df267e0d0d89c8b5e587c1ae3fafd7b9306ef1</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T02:44:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-venezuela-to-join-g20-energy-meetings-in-texas-at-us-invitation--7120fef6df3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-venezuela-to-join-g20-energy-meetings-in-texas-at-us-invitation" /><summary type="html">A Venezuelan delegation will join G20 energy talks in Houston this week as soaring oil prices and disruption from the Middle East war put global energy supplies under pressure. The meeting comes as the Trump administration deepens energy ties with Caracas and seeks to boost Venezuelan oil output.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court rejects Trump bid to restrict mail ballots as voting begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d86d5cb8d8231f84ea0118119fc5d587eb79a8b806d9bed75b2b8230beee58f</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T01:51:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-ballots-as-voting-begins--73bfd34fa579.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-ballots-as-voting-begins" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court on Monday rejected President Donald Trump’s bid to impose new restrictions on mail ballots ahead of November’s midterm elections. The ruling leaves states free to continue using existing voting procedures, after election officials warned the last-minute changes could disrupt ballot distribution.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Rapper Macklemore dropped from Ed Sheeran's US tour after pro-Palestinian remarks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b9dacea53b9c59578ca62dce83a73d2c76f415ce4554eb2e807c0e2cfab5090</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T22:20:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-macklemore-dropped-from-ed-sheeran-us-tour-after-pro-palestinian-remarks--73709c875802.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-macklemore-dropped-from-ed-sheeran-us-tour-after-pro-palestinian-remarks" /><summary type="html">British singer Ed Sheeran responded on Tuesday to American rapper Macklemore being dropped from his US stadium tour after saying "Free Palestine" during a September 4 concert in New Jersey. The Grammy winner’s removal follows pressure from venue owners, including New England Patriots owner Robert Kraft, over his criticism of Israel’s actions in Gaza.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Space Force confirms weapons deployed in space for first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c681ab3ae9ce5b14d1178cc1072ddd7ca085dcb4809ee196c40b4c986834136f</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-space-force-confirms-weapons-deployed-in-space-for-first-time--b77423806d11.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-space-force-confirms-weapons-deployed-in-space-for-first-time" /><summary type="html">The US Space Force on Monday confirmed for the first time that Washington has weapons deployed in orbit, as the United States, China and Russia expand their military capabilities in space. The disclosure highlights a growing focus on controlling the space domain and protecting satellites vital to military communications, surveillance and navigation.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump criticises 'negative forces' seeking to slow AI development</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab39970ca5454309c78c21256838b0fa93a80ccf27cf436c1355fb7f1cb0e6e1</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:49:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-trump-criticises-negative-forces-seeking-to-slow-ai-development--bd4a498a26cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-trump-criticises-negative-forces-seeking-to-slow-ai-development" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday slammed critics of artificial intelligence (AI) who warned firms to slow down development, branding them "negative" forces. The comments came soon after OpenAI CEO Sam Altman announced his company will not go public this year, citing safety concerns.</summary></entry><entry><title>US hosts G20 energy talks in Texas as Iran war disrupts global fuel markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc015af21fdc93fb2553355ddf50cf995ae8f7db86ab6fedfba4eb30abeaa785</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T01:42:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-g20-energy-talks-iran-war--39ce092f6892.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-g20-energy-talks-iran-war" /><summary type="html">The United States begins G20 meetings in Houston on Monday promoting “energy abundance” as President Donald Trump’s war against Iran disrupts global fuel markets. Delegations from major economies, including China, India, Japan and Germany, will attend alongside oil producers Canada and Saudi Arabia. Russia is also expected to participate.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>‘I gave up my life to care for my father’: How 9/11 shaped a son’s sense of duty and life trajectory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3555e559afd25f862e10fb249cf2c8019b8992051b63d3dad0647cde12bf34c9</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T17:10:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/i-gave-up-my-life-to-care-for-my-father-how-9-11-shaped-a-son-s-sense-of-duty-and-life-trajectory--da02b8721d79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/i-gave-up-my-life-to-care-for-my-father-how-9-11-shaped-a-son-s-sense-of-duty-and-life-trajectory" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Alessandro Stravato, a witness to the attacks of September 11th. His testimony offers a deeply personal account. He witnessed firsthand the second plane strike the World Trade Center from Arthur Ashe Stadium. Stravato’s first instinct was not to interpret the historical significance, just find his father, who was working at City Hall.  He found him alive, covered in debris and soot, trekking dozens of blocks through Manhattan. And while his father did survive, his health seriously deteriorated over the years. By 2015, as Alessandro's dad was losing his battle with cancer, he told his son to "stay strong."</summary></entry><entry><title>‘We did what we had to do’: 25 years on, 9/11 first responder reflects on duty, survival and family</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8547aee8b4b661a9fae437730e975356fdd997ae0f068bbcf95db624aa54d515</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T16:18:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/we-did-what-we-had-to-do-25-years-on-9-11-first-responder-reflects-on-duty-survival-and-family--5b4d9acc4527.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/we-did-what-we-had-to-do-25-years-on-9-11-first-responder-reflects-on-duty-survival-and-family" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome LaZetta Duncan, Retired NYPD Detective, 9/11 First Responder. Duncan remembers Ground Zero not as a historical event frozen in time, but as living history whose consequences continue to unfold and evolve 25 years on. Her testimony traces a striking progression: from the confusion and urgency of the attacks, rescue and recovery, to the grim transformation of gathering human remains and evidence inside a burning toxic apocalyptic crime scene. And we now learn of the overwhelming health consequences borne by responders despite repeated assurances that the air quality posed no health threat.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Michelle Bolsonaro's key role in the presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c4c3c6aa862df5f9bcd577b3101e2a2586f83268afa684077ba3b6222000dda</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:08:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race--c6d331e45ad7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">Brazil is heading to the polls on October 4, with President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva seeking a fourth term as the Bolsonaro family mounts a political comeback through Flávio's presidential bid and Michelle's Senate campaign. With polls pointing to another tight race, Michelle's popularity among women could prove crucial as the family tries to return to power.</summary></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: 9/11 anniversary, far-right win in Germany and Houthis' Yemen offensive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9cefa906b64b85328595def7b49745a1daf8b1fec13abe1ca1bb8d33058dc14</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T10:48:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive--652ff4e85a45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive" /><summary type="html">A look back at some of the week's key news stories and the most striking images, from commemorations marking 25 years since the 9/11 attacks to the breakthrough win for Germany's far-right AfD party and the lightening offensive that has left Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels in control of the country's Red Sea coast.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Macron, Carney to visit North Atlantic French islands after Trump's map post</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4d139182a19b55903df96489c7b10dd6a46f22f799d74f31cd6ea1572c4eced</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:25:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-macron-carney-to-visit-french-islands-after-trump-s-map-post--f17f71093187.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-macron-carney-to-visit-french-islands-after-trump-s-map-post" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney will reaffirm the “sovereignty of nations” on a visit on September 20 to Saint-Pierre-et-Miquelon, a French territory in the North Atlantic, the Élysée Palace announced on Sunday. The symbolic trip comes after US President Donald Trump posted a map on social media showing the entire North American continent covered by the US flag.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>On Sept 12th, 'everyone was compassionate': The world needs 'to be together again' - Richard Roeill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94004352322065408207e78810ebb36816609c21324f16f58d1cda55c6f8c2e3</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T07:18:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-on-sept-12th-everyone-was-compassionate-the-world-needs-to-be-together-again-richard-roeill--bad1381d87fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-on-sept-12th-everyone-was-compassionate-the-world-needs-to-be-together-again-richard-roeill" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24’s François Picard talks to Richard Roeill, former New York Firefighter and 9/11 First Responder. Roeill’s testimony reframes the legacy of September 11th not as a historical event confined to a single day, but as living history. The former New York City firefighter describes an anniversary that reactivates trauma, while the illnesses suffered by first responders make the consequences of Ground Zero ever-present decades later. He says that responders were misled about the dangers they faced and demands accountability and long-term healthcare for those exposed to the toxic air.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Can we slow down AI, and who has the right to remember 9/11?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a405c1b27ee801dac30cf154ac0161baf34a7b2d2651163001a93c3100f1ccc5</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T18:43:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260911-can-we-slowdown-ai-and-9-11-who-has-the-right-to-remember--b55b74262dd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260911-can-we-slowdown-ai-and-9-11-who-has-the-right-to-remember" /><summary type="html">In a week that marks 25 years since 9/11, Americans paused to pay tribute. Six bells tolled to signify six fatal moments in New York, at the Pentagon and in Pennsylvania– with a seventh bell rung this year to commemorate those who later died from 9/11-related illnesses.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>US government has decided on 'Guantanamo forever'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62b2a247f842ec2af80f1836f35e7afe5eb6bca50ca96c591b1de90d8147e69a</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T18:42:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260911-spotlight--86e38a56a856.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260911-spotlight" /><summary type="html">In this edition, FRANCE 24’s Gavin Lee speaks to New York Times reporter Carol Rosenberg, widely regarded as one of the foremost American journalists covering the US detention camp at Guantanamo Bay in Cuba. Several alleged suspects in the 9/11 attacks are still being held there, including their so-called “architect”, Khalid Sheikh Mohammed. He is scheduled for trial in June 2028, 27 years after the tragedy. To mark the anniversary, Rosenberg has written a reflective piece titled A Place Where Memories Have Faded Away.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry></feed>
